  "full_text": "I, the Lord of sea and sky, I have heard my people cry. All who dwell in dark and sin, my hand will save. I who made the stars at night, I will make their darkness bright. I will set a feast for them, whom shall I send? Here I am, Lord. Is it I, Lord? I have heard you calling in the night. I will go, Lord, if you lead me. I will hold your people in my heart. I, the Lord of sea and rain. I will send them fire and rain. I will tend the poor and lame. I will mend their hearts of stone. Give them hearts for love alone. Here I am, Lord. Is it I, Lord? I have heard you calling in the night. I will go, Lord, if you lead me. I will hold your people in my heart.",
